hello and welcome to the new world  viewer source for everything anime and  manga and we are back to talk about what  this anti-magic child does before  during and indeed after spats of yelling  seriously i'm only reading the manga and  i am getting hit with the full  force of asta's vocal range but more  specifically we are here to talk about  arc  number three of black clover which i  believe is named the royal capital r  another very fun and surprising set of  chapters that give me that very familiar  feeling of starting off in quite a  generic place before taking those  concepts one step further than your  average shown shonen series and i really  enjoyed this arc actually honestly  probably not quite as much as the  dungeon exploration but there is a ton  to digest here regardless and before i  engage in digestion please do take a  moment to digest this request to  subscribe to the new old review as per  usual i probably won't be reading these  comments due to fear of spoilers so  subscribing through this video and  liking this video are the only ways i  can really tell if you want more of  black  clover but the premise of our third arc  goes as follows after doing some  seriously  cool stuff in the dungeon asta yuno and  friends of astor and yuno are invited to  the royal capital in order to file a  report with mr wizardking himself and  while they're here they meet all sorts  of nobility and general high-ranking  mages some of which are pricks some of  which are amazing and others are just  meh so meh that they may as well not  even be there however everyone must then  work together when the capital is  attacked by dark magical cultists led  by crazy people it's a fine premise the  stating of which does the ark no justice  whatsoever because just as with the  previous arc most of the substance here  lies with internal character evolution  intriguing interactions  and the overall theme of the arc which  is benchmarking and we're going to start  this discussion with the latter because  in practically every shonen series the  plucky young protagonist  will eventually hit a wall something  that their unique power and relentless  determination is simply  unable to overcome in any circumstances  thus giving them a benchmark to surpass  in the future  now black clover takes that concept a  step further with the royal capital arc  and while subtle  it gives us a road map for going forward  with an almost step-by-step guide as to  how either asta or yuno is going to  become the wizard king and it begins  pretty damn immediately by showcasing  the magic knight ranking system which is  very simple but very effective there are  five grand ranks and within each of  those five they are divided into a  further five subclasses  it's a lot of fives there but assuming  that the wizard king does not have that  subclass system this would give us  20 levels of magic night progress that  we will need to travel through before  the idea  of wizard king becomes anywhere near  tangible and i love this by the way  because i said this in the last video  but i crave rules and structure the last  dark provided that for magic and this  arc provides that for organizational  structure now with that said how does  this help us in regards to asda well  it's tricky because he doesn't seem to  initially fit anywhere here given that  his current rank isn't mentioned to the  best of my knowledge maybe it didn't i  missed it but i would have to assume  that he is a junior magic knight fifth  class aka the lowest of the ranks but  technical definitions are  only half of the truth here in reality  tarbita does something very interesting  to kind of let us know where asta is  power wise and that comes in the  character of leopold it might be quite a  comical aspect of the arc but leopold  declares asta his rival and throughout  the ensuing events these two are often  depicted as equals especially at the end  where they're both fighting like rapid  animals and leopold just so happens to  be an intermediate magic knight  second class so regardless of any  official ranking this seems to me about  where asta sits which is a step or two  above entry level but he still has a  long way to go  and from there our next benchmark is  seen in the squad captains asta is  thoroughly outclassed by both juego leon  and nozzle meanwhile these two are shown  to be thoroughly outclassed by the power  of the wizard king who is himself  also potentially outclassed by the  mystery villain at the end of the arc  thus giving us these really tangible  steps to be taken by astor and yuno we  now have something to benchmark them  against going forward and this arc  essentially allows us to track their  progress on a chart if we so saw fit  it's not just aster and you know either  most of the key characters in this arc  have some sort of benchmark set for them  leopold for example is now very directly  on a quest to surpass fuego leon and  even become the wizard king himself and  you know what even noel has a new  benchmark which  is admittedly minor but it is present  and it is simply not to remain weak  which is one of the best lines in the  arc actually when fuego leon tells her  that being weak is nothing to be ashamed  of but staying weak is  i really love that what i did not love  however is both noel and mimosa all of a  sudden being all smitten with  asta because i hate this trope so so  much i mean yeah i enjoyed it as a  teenager  i don't know though as a man in his  early 30s there is a limit to how much i  can tolerate awkwardly written love  struck 15 year old girls and i really  really really hope this isn't how  they're both going to be going forward  for the next  i don't know however long this series is  but now we're introduced to a whole ton  of new characters in this arc which i  think is both a good  and a bad thing on the one hand i really  love that tabitha is consistently  filling this world with as much  content as he can muster which in this  case comes in the form of an ass ton of  characters  i like it because it winds our focus  beyond the asta centric groups but at  times that focus can get a bit too wide  even for me  one example would be early on when we  see all of the magic knights receiving  their promotions  we see leopold get his and that's nice  then we see seoul get hers and that's  also nice but then you turn the page and  it's just this  two-page spread of like five other  people being promoted one by one  and i just stopped caring immediately  for the most part it was fine though i  don't mind these unique faces popping up  and not being explored too deeply  because that just effectively fills the  world  just please no more two-page spreads of  people i don't care about being promoted  and i will say this feeling also extends  into some of the action of the arc  there's a part near the beginning of all  of the fighting where we have like  six pages in a row of prominent magic  nights just firing off their mage  juices and if i stop and look at all of  the panels they're all cool in their own  way but after like the third page of  watching around a magic knight unload a  spell i was kind of over it because to  me that really killed the pacing of the  chapter  action is supposed to be fast and  exciting you know one or two bursts  would have been great however when we  linger and go through  every single mages opening attack one by  one  over the course of six pages then it  makes me feel like i'm stuck in the  wizard king's chronostasis spell like  i'm living in this one  unending moment and given that most of  these spells are shown later on in the  arc anyway you really didn't need to  cram them all in here because not only  did it slow everything down but tabitha  also blew his load for revealing them in  a more exciting way later on anyway  that's enough negativity let's move on  and talk about some negativity so some  of these new characters just so happen  to be noel's relatives and they're quite  essential here two older brothers and  one older sister of house silver and i  hate these people  each and every single one of them can go  screw themselves in the most  uncomfortable way possible however i  love this dynamic  i hate them because they're designed to  be hated and it leads to a great moment  with asda telling them all to f off  early on and you know not in those words  but it is nice to see the underdog put  these pricks in their place  with that said noel's relatives do have  one redeeming feature so far in nozzle  he has a brief flashback at the end of  the arc to highlight his camaraderie and  or rivalry with juego leon  and that was really nice in many ways  yes he is still a complete and utter  [ __ ] but at least he has a lot more  depth than the other over the [ __ ]  and speaking of juego leon i've brought  him up a lot already but i love him the  moment where he told astor that you and  i are rivals as well is all i needed to  sell me on him he is absolutely  fantastic in every way which is of  course why he had to be hurt hurt  quite badly even because we care about  him and that makes him a very effective  target for drama and as for those who  were doing the hurting the main villains  of this arc aren't quite as interesting  to me as lotus and mars i think those  two really were something special but  i suppose these guys will do i mean  rydez had an intriguing inferiority  complex going on trying to prove himself  to be better than all of the nobles who  would look down upon him and on top of  that  the dude only had one spell i mean what  a loser but also not really because he  does of course remind me a lot of asda  looked down upon  cast aside and really only has this one  narrow yet incredibly effective talent  radez has asked her if he went down a  darker road which i guess he is pursuing  the power of what may be a literal devil  so we'll see about that but in regards  to writers his magic was also quite  interesting i do like how he managed to  use his one spell to provide this  amazing level of versatility and i did  also  quite like his design i just wasn't 100  sold on him though i understand his  motivation to a degree  you know getting revenge on the pompous  people that's always a good one but  there is a massive gap between that and  you know trying to murder children for  fun  all in all he was just a bit more  generically evil than i would have liked  and a bit less interesting as a result  and i'd say the same for old lady who i  think is named catherine i prefer what  you know caught her though and actually  don't really know what to say about her  i mean  she was there she was certainly there  and there was even a third one as well  it doesn't matter something that  is important is that they all seem to  know about asta's auntie magic and i  want to know how to my knowledge that's  not something that's been widely  publicized and really the only people  who should know are those within the  magic knights or those who took and  failed the exam  which i suppose may mean we have a  traitor in our midst which is always fun  if so and in regards to other things  yuno was understated but fantastic  during the sock he got deprived of his  five senses and learned to connect with  his new fairy friend  who is apparently silf a mightily opie  win spirit and one of the four great  attributes which does excite me because  i now eagerly await the discovery of the  other three  and as for the wizard king himself i  still don't really know how to feel  about him he's quite charming and  eccentric whilst also harboring this  fairly terrifying potential not just in  terms of raw power but his beliefs can  be fairly harsh as well like when he  just up and murdered some fools stating  that well they were prepared to die  right as well as almost appearing to  take pleasure in the idea of torturing  them through the cronus stasis spell so  at the moment i really don't quite see  him as the role model aster does because  this dude has some pretty damn dark  features in addition to that apparently  there is a non-wizard king in this world  as well someone who prefers to be  adorned by mysterious shrouds and many  many  assumedly beautiful human females and he  seems to be set up to be a pretty  obvious bad dude dick right now but i  suppose it's nice to know that magic  isn't everything in this world like it's  not as if the wizard king just rules the  entire nation like i initially thought  he might oh and also charmy was here i  like her she's cute and furiously  powerful  she had nothing to do with anything but  she was admittedly a nice break from all  of the serious business happening  elsewhere but yeah the royal capital arc  was quite good overall it was much more  of a mixed bag than the dungeon  exploration one but i'm quite glad that  asterisk hit his wall now because we can  begin working on getting beyond that and  slowly working our way up the tier  system that has been set up for us but  that pretty much does it for this blind  review of the royal capital arc and what  do you guys think please do leave your  thoughts in the comments below or even  join my discord server and if you're  keen for some more black clover content  then please do go and check out some of  my other videos or even subscribe to the  channel  for very maybe black clover goodness  delivered straight into your youtube  feed but for now this has been the new  world review  and i'll see you next time

